* Behavioral contract for the battery-port hardware PWM interlock.
* IPRI is a simulator proxy in volts per ampere. All logic pins use 0/1 V.
* BIAS_OK aggregates the required gate-bias and protection-supply power-good signals.
.subckt PORT_TRIP IPRI BIAS_OK ARM RUN PERMIT G params: ITRIP=125
Bfault fault G V={abs(v(IPRI,G)) >= ITRIP || v(BIAS_OK,G) < 0.5}
Bsafe safe G V={v(RUN,G) < 0.5 && v(fault,G) < 0.5}
* XSPICE bridges are ground referenced. Translate all logic at the interface.
Bdata data 0 V={v(safe,G)}
Bclock clk 0 V={v(ARM,G)}
Breset rst 0 V={v(fault,G)}
Alogic [data clk rst] [ddata dclk drst] trip_adc
.model trip_adc adc_bridge(in_low=0.3 in_high=0.7)
* Rising-edge arm. Asynchronous reset revokes authorization on any trip.
Alatch ddata dclk NULL drst dq NULL trip_ff
.model trip_ff d_dff(ic=0 clk_delay=2n reset_delay=2n)
Astate [dq] [armed] trip_dac
.model trip_dac dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high=1 out_undef=0 t_rise=2n t_fall=2n)
Bpermit PERMIT G V={v(armed) > 0.7 && v(RUN,G) > 0.7 && v(fault,G) < 0.3}
.ends PORT_TRIP
